  "title": "sEEG Forced Two-Choice Task",
  "description": "Stereoelectroencephalography (sEEG) recordings from patients performing a forced two-choice response task in the epilepsy monitoring unit at Oregon Health & Science University. The data were analyzed in collaboration with the University of Oregon and used to characterize movement-related oscillations across brain regions sampled by intracranial electrodes. The accompanying data paper (Rockhill, Mantovani, Stedelin, Nerison, Raslan, & Swann; Journal of Neural Engineering) describes the dataset and analyses; note that C. S. Nerison appears in that paper's author list but not in the BIDS dataset_description.json.",
  "methods_description": "Stereoelectroencephalography was recorded from patients in an epilepsy monitoring unit while they performed a forced two-choice response task. Data were organized according to the iEEG-BIDS specification using MNE-BIDS.",
